"}},{"id":"romanian_deadlift_barbell","name":"romanian_deadlift_barbell","description":"The royal exercise for the body's posterior chain, targeting the hamstrings and glutes. Key to controlled hip hinging for strength development and injury prevention.","difficulty":7,"category":"strength","equipment":["weights"],"primary_muscle":"Legs – Hamstrings","secondary_muscles":["Glutes","Back","Abs / Core"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S4","glutes":"S8","legs_hamstrings":"P10","back":"S7","forearms_(front)":"S4"}},{"id":"running","name":"running","description":"The most natural form of movement for improving cardiovascular endurance and burning calories. Running activates the whole body, strengthens the heart, and improves overall well-being.","difficulty":5,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Cardio","secondary_muscles":["Legs – Quads","Calves","Glutes"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S3","calves":"P7","legs_quads":"P8","glutes":"S6","legs_hamstrings":"S6","cardio":"P10"}},{"id":"russian_twist","name":"russian_twist","description":"A dynamic rotational exercise focusing on the oblique abdominal muscles. By creating stability during rotation, you will build a strong and defined midsection.","difficulty":4,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Back","Legs – Quads"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P9","shoulders":"S3","legs_quads":"S3","back":"S3","cardio":"T3"}},{"id":"russian_twist_weighted_ball","name":"russian_twist_weighted_ball","description":"An upgrade of the classic Russian twist using a medicine ball or weight. The added resistance increases the load on the abdominal muscles and shoulders, leading to greater strength and endurance.","difficulty":5,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Back","Legs – Quads"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P10","shoulders":"S4","legs_quads":"S3","back":"S4","cardio":"T4"}},{"id":"scapula_push_up","name":"scapula_push_up","description":"A simple yet extremely effective exercise for scapular stabilization and strengthening the muscles that support the shoulder girdle. Ideal as a warm-up or rehabilitation exercise.","difficulty":3,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Shoulders","secondary_muscles":["Back","Abs / Core"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S4","shoulders":"P7","chest":"S3","triceps":"S3","back":"S6"}},{"id":"scissors_kick","name":"scissors_kick","description":"A scissors-kick leg exercise that relentlessly targets the lower abdominal muscles and hip flexors. Keeping the legs low above the floor ensures maximum tension.","difficulty":4,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Legs – Quads","Legs – Hamstrings"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P9","legs_quads":"S5","legs_hamstrings":"S3","cardio":"T4"}},{"id":"shadow_boxing","name":"shadow_boxing","description":"Shadow boxing is an excellent way to improve coordination, speed, and cardiovascular endurance. It activates the shoulders and core while relieving stress.","difficulty":4,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Cardio","secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Abs / Core","Triceps"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S5","shoulders":"P7","calves":"S4","chest":"S4","triceps":"S5","legs_quads":"S3","back":"S3","biceps":"S3","cardio":"P9"}},{"id":"shoulder_abduction","name":"shoulder_abduction","description":"Lateral arm raises for activating the middle deltoids. The exercise is key for shoulder joint mobility and proper upper body posture.","difficulty":2,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Shoulders","secondary_muscles":["Back"],"muscle_intensity":{"shoulders":"P8","stretching":"T3","back":"S4"}},{"id":"shoulder_circle","name":"shoulder_circle","description":"Shoulder circles are a basic warm-up exercise for releasing tension in the neck and upper back. They increase blood flow to the shoulder joint and prepare the body for effort.","difficulty":1,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Shoulders","secondary_muscles":["Stretching","Back"],"muscle_intensity":{"shoulders":"P9","stretching":"P8","back":"S3"}},{"id":"shoulder_extension","name":"shoulder_extension","description":"Pushing the arms backward strengthens the rear deltoids and upper back. This movement helps correct posture in those who spend a lot of time at a computer.","difficulty":2,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Shoulders","secondary_muscles":["Back","Triceps"],"muscle_intensity":{"shoulders":"P8","triceps":"S4","stretching":"T2","back":"S6"}},{"id":"side_plank","name":"side_plank","description":"An isometric exercise that builds unbreakable core stability and strengthens the lateral abdominal muscles. The side plank is essential for anyone who wants to protect the spine and improve balance.","difficulty":5,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Glutes","Back"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P10","shoulders":"S6","legs_quads":"S3","glutes":"S5","back":"S4"}},{"id":"side_plank_oblique_crunch","name":"side_plank_oblique_crunch","description":"Combines the stability of the side plank with active trunk flexion. Touching the upper elbow to the knee will maximally load the lateral abdominal muscles.","difficulty":6,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Glutes","Legs – Quads"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P10","shoulders":"S7","legs_quads":"S4","glutes":"S6","back":"S4","cardio":"T3"}},{"id":"side_plank_with_hip_lift","name":"side_plank_with_hip_lift","description":"Hip lifts in the side plank add a dynamic component that further loads the oblique abdominal muscles. Great for shaping the waist and strengthening the hips.","difficulty":6,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Glutes","Shoulders","Back"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P10","shoulders":"S6","legs_quads":"S3","glutes":"S6","back":"S4","cardio":"T2"}},{"id":"side_push_up","name":"side_push_up","description":"An unusual yet effective push-up variation performed lying on your side. It mainly targets the triceps and chest muscles on one side of the body, helping to correct muscular imbalances.","difficulty":5,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Triceps","secondary_muscles":["Chest","Shoulders","Abs / Core"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S4","shoulders":"S5","chest":"P8","triceps":"P9"}},{"id":"side_to_side_punch","name":"side_to_side_punch","description":"Rapid sideward punches activate your cardiovascular system and strengthen the shoulders. Trunk rotation ensures the abdominal muscles are also engaged in the work.","difficulty":3,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Cardio","secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Abs / Core","Triceps"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S6","shoulders":"P7","calves":"S3","chest":"S3","triceps":"S5","legs_quads":"S3","back":"S3","cardio":"P8"}},{"id":"side_to_side_push_up","name":"side_to_side_push_up","description":"An advanced push-up variation where you alternately shift weight from one side to the other. This creates greater stress on each side of the chest and requires better core stability.","difficulty":6,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Chest","secondary_muscles":["Shoulders","Triceps","Abs / Core"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S5","shoulders":"S7","chest":"P9","triceps":"S7","back":"S4","cardio":"T4"}},{"id":"single_leg_calf_raise_leg_press_machine","name":"single_leg_calf_raise_leg_press_machine","description":"An isolation exercise for strong and defined calves on the leg press machine. Unilateral execution allows complete concentration on the muscle and eliminates differences in strength between legs.","difficulty":5,"category":"strength","equipment":["weights"],"primary_muscle":"Calves","secondary_muscles":["Legs – Quads"],"muscle_intensity":{"calves":"P10","legs_quads":"S3","stretching":"T4"}},{"id":"situps","name":"situps","description":"A classic exercise for strengthening the entire abdominal wall. Controlled trunk raises will increase core stability and hip flexor strength.","difficulty":4,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Abs / Core","secondary_muscles":["Legs – Quads"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"P9","legs_quads":"S4","cardio":"T2"}},{"id":"skipping","name":"skipping","description":"Jump rope skipping is a top cardio exercise for rapid calorie burn. It improves coordination, endurance, and explosive calf strength.","difficulty":4,"category":"strength","equipment":["bodyweight"],"primary_muscle":"Cardio","secondary_muscles":["Calves","Legs – Quads","Abs / Core"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S5","shoulders":"S4","calves":"P9","legs_quads":"S6","glutes":"S5","legs_hamstrings":"S4","cardio":"P10","forearms_(front)":"T2"}},{"id":"smith_machine_bulgarian_split_squat","name":"smith_machine_bulgarian_split_squat","description":"One of the most effective lower body isolation exercises in the stable environment of a Smith machine. Emphasizes quad development and deep glute activation.","difficulty":6,"category":"strength","equipment":["weights"],"primary_muscle":"Legs – Quads","secondary_muscles":["Glutes","Legs – Hamstrings","Abs / Core"],"muscle_intensity":{"abs_/_core":"S4","calves":"S3","legs_quads":"P10","glutes":"S8","legs_hamstrings":"S6","stretching":"T2","cardio":"T3"}},{"id":"smith_machine_calf_raise","name":"smith_machine_calf_raise","description":"Precise calf isolation with additional load. The Smith machine guides the weight, allowing maximum focus on calf muscle contraction and stretching.","difficulty":4,